 name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9169696-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9169696</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1067111A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEM</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INA TOMOHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INA, TOMOHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INA TOMOHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INA, TOMOHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process which comprises subjecting a reaction mixture containing a hydroquinone diester derivative represented by formula (1) (wherein R&lt;1&gt; and R&lt;2&gt; are the same or different and each represents alkyl, cycloalkyl, aryl, or a heterocyclic group) to crystallisation and washing the resultant crystals. The crystallization is conducted in a solvent comprising an organic carboxylic acid and water, and the crystals are washed with warm water having a temperature of 40 DEG C or higher. In formula (1), R&lt;1&gt; and R&lt;2&gt; is C1-4 alkyl.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Le procédé de la présente invention consiste à prendre un mélange de réaction, à le soumettre à cristallisation, et à rincer les cristaux résultants. Ce mélange de réaction contient un dérivé d'hydroquinone-diester représenté par la formule générale (1). Dans cette formule générale (1), R&lt;1&gt; et R&lt;2&gt;, qui sont identiques ou différents, sont chacun alkyle, cycloalkyle, aryle, ou un groupe hétérocyclique. On réalise la cristallisation dans un solvant d'eau et d'acide carboxylique organique. Le rinçage des cristaux se fait dans une eau tiède faisant au moins 40 DEG C. En l'espèce, dans la formule générale (1), R&lt;1&gt; et R&lt;2&gt; sont C1-C4 alkyle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>